  ! #lexer
    # Lexer
    p MaxUp uses a single-byte ASCII token set for maximum keystroke efficiency.
    p The most common HTML elements are mapped to single characters:
    ; .token-table
      = 
      ` Token ` Element ` Mnemonic
      = 
      ` @     ` a       ` at
      ` %     ` img     ` percent
      ` ;     ` div     ` semicolon
      ` :     ` span    ` colon
      ` +     ` button  ` positive action
      ` ?     ` input   ` question
      ` ?=    ` form    ` form
      ` p     ` p       ` paragraph
      ` #     ` h1      ` heading
      ` (     ` ul      ` group
      ` -     ` li      ` list item
      ` ^     ` table   ` caret
      ` \"`\"     ` td      ` backtick
      ` =     ` tr      ` equals row
  ! #parser
    # Parser
    p MaxUp uses indentation-based nesting. Children are determined by whitespace indentation levels.
    p Attributes use key=value syntax. Classes use .classname.
    ; .example
      p Example:
      ; .card
        p {{ title }}
        + on:click="handleClick" "Click me"
  ! #emitter
    # Emitter
    p MaxUp compiles to multiple targets:
    ( 
      - HTML5 .mu
      - Leptos RSX/WASM .rs
      - Python SPRAG .py
      - MaxUp Bytecode .maxc
    )
